<pending_commit branch="chromeos-2015.07" change_id="I6a3a15feb6edd355d6ec252c36b6f7885b383099" commit="d903be7120e2094cdf5674fb824dbd89d501f674" commit_message="UPSTREAM: cbfs/vboot: remove firmware component support  The Chrome OS verified boot path supported multiple CBFS instances in the boot media as well as stand-alone assets sitting in each vboot RW slot. Remove the support for the stand-alone assets and always use CBFS accesses as the way to retrieve data.  This is implemented by adding a cbfs_locator object which is queried for locating the current CBFS. Additionally, it is also signalled prior to when a program is about to be loaded by coreboot for the subsequent stage/payload. This provides the same opportunity as previous for vboot to hook in and perform its logic.  BUG=chromium:445938 BRANCH=None TEST=Built and ran on glados. CQ-DEPEND=CL:307121,CL:316960,CL:316961  Original-Reviewed-on: https://review.coreboot.org/12689 Original-Tested-by: build bot (Jenkins) Original-Tested-by: Raptor Engineering Automated Test Stand &lt;noreply@raptorengineeringinc.com&gt; Original-Reviewed-by: Patrick Georgi &lt;pgeorgi@google.com&gt; Original-Reviewed-by: Stefan Reinauer &lt;stefan.reinauer@coreboot.org&gt; (cherry picked from commit 6d720f38e06d14cc8a89635f66dc124dcd5ac150)  Change-Id: I6a3a15feb6edd355d6ec252c36b6f7885b383099 Signed-off-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/316950 Reviewed-by: Patrick Georgi &lt;pgeorgi@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="3" gerrit_number="316950" owner_email="adurbin@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="16" project="chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" ref="refs/changes/50/316950/16" remote="cros" total_fail_count="9"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I3003afd029408fa984515d8ecc7c5c5309f53bdc" commit="a8927533c81a2f3602b7be1ec2e19552ce766ea4" commit_message="Enable use of CBFS in RW sections  This switches boards over to use CBFS-formatted FW_MAIN_*, and gets rid of (EC|PD)_MAIN_[AB] in the process.  With several changes in other repositories (incl. upstream coreboot), this leads to a working image that jumps to RW and finds its EC firmware in CBFS, too.  BUG=chromium:445938 BRANCH=tot TEST=none CQ-DEPEND=CL:316950  Change-Id: I3003afd029408fa984515d8ecc7c5c5309f53bdc Signed-off-by: Patrick Georgi &lt;pgeorgi@google.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/307121 Commit-Ready: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Patrick Georgi &lt;pgeorgi@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Daisuke Nojiri &lt;dnojiri@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="307121" owner_email="pgeorgi@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="12" project="chromiumos/platform/depthcharge" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/depthcharge" ref="refs/changes/21/307121/12" remote="cros" total_fail_count="11"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ife5ec2c72e8263f83030a079367e7c52b016ef4a" commit="8a47322c9e863cba1a3af4c9185b2a98df597765" commit_message="Handle multiple CBFS cleanly  libpayload already honors the lb_boot_media_params found in the coreboot tables when CBFS_DEFAULT_MEDIA is used. Therefore, no extra code is required to deal with multiple CBFS instances within a RW or an RO slot.  BUG=chromium:445938 BRANCH=None TEST=Built and ran on glados. CQ-DEPEND=CL:316950  Change-Id: Ife5ec2c72e8263f83030a079367e7c52b016ef4a Signed-off-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/316960 Tested-by: Patrick Georgi &lt;pgeorgi@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Patrick Georgi &lt;pgeorgi@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="2" gerrit_number="316960" owner_email="adurbin@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="7" project="chromiumos/platform/depthcharge" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/depthcharge" ref="refs/changes/60/316960/7" remote="cros" total_fail_count="8"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I8854dbbb061219d63498325280419bd489185b8e" commit="f49442ce181e1d4ac4027a670ceca984a38e4748" commit_message="Remove firmware components from vboot_handoff.  coreboot droppped firmware component support in the vboot_handoff struct when moving over to only support multiple CBFS instances. Therefore, update the vboot_handoff structure to match coreboot.  BUG=chromium:445938 BRANCH=None TEST=Built and ran on glados. CQ-DEPEND=CL:316950  Change-Id: I8854dbbb061219d63498325280419bd489185b8e Signed-off-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/316961 Tested-by: Patrick Georgi &lt;pgeorgi@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Randall Spangler &lt;rspangler@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Patrick Georgi &lt;pgeorgi@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="316961" owner_email="adurbin@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="7" project="chromiumos/platform/depthcharge" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/depthcharge" ref="refs/changes/61/316961/7" remote="cros" total_fail_count="7"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-2015.07" change_id="I383fd6579280cf9cfe5a18c2851baf74cad004e9" commit="044f39542ecfebab75e392e026891e273229aba9" commit_message="UPSTREAM: lib: remove assets infrastructure  Now that only CBFS access is supported for finding resources within the boot media the assets infrastructure can be removed. Remove it.  BUG=chromium:445938 BRANCH=None TEST=Built and ran on glados.  Original-Reviewed-on: https://review.coreboot.org/12690 Original-Tested-by: build bot (Jenkins) Original-Reviewed-by: Patrick Georgi &lt;pgeorgi@google.com&gt; Original-Reviewed-by: Stefan Reinauer &lt;stefan.reinauer@coreboot.org&gt; (cherry picked from commit 7e7a4df58075fdff4293d2203b035b970d21aeb8)  Change-Id: I383fd6579280cf9cfe5a18c2851baf74cad004e9 Signed-off-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/316951 Reviewed-by: Patrick Georgi &lt;pgeorgi@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="2" gerrit_number="316951" owner_email="adurbin@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="16" project="chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" ref="refs/changes/51/316951/16" remote="cros" total_fail_count="8"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I898f7d70e09124ec261c3eb5029ca1abb6b9a51d" commit="052efa2c19560a83fa00b329f03ac1f34f2d7649" commit_message="Collect more debug information for failures  This CL adds in some code to dump the raw touch events to disk as the firmware test suite runs.  This is useful in the situation where the test hangs or crashes due to unexpected input.  Previously there was no way to analyize what input broke the test suite other than (hopefully) a stack trace. With this CL now there is a log saved to disk will all the events that were leading up to the failure.  BUG=none TEST=manually tested and used to debug a failure.  Change-Id: I898f7d70e09124ec261c3eb5029ca1abb6b9a51d Signed-off-by: Charlie Mooney &lt;charliemooney@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/320462 Reviewed-by: Shyh-In Hwang &lt;josephsih@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="320462" owner_email="charliemooney@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/touch_firmware_test" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/touch_firmware_test" ref="refs/changes/62/320462/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ib81476eee4c9de921502a3a47f6990b9e6b1968b" commit="baf022fde5840ae241e80fdec2c0a7e88078595e" commit_message="Update a utility to support the new tpm sysfs class directory  Kernel TPM patches from 4.x moved /sys/class/misc/tpm0 to /sys/class/tpm/tpm0. Support both paths in this utility.  BUG=chromium:573368 BRANCH=none TEST=untested, not sure if this utility is still used.  Change-Id: Ib81476eee4c9de921502a3a47f6990b9e6b1968b Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/320892 Commit-Ready: Bryan Freed &lt;bfreed@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Bryan Freed &lt;bfreed@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Duncan Laurie &lt;dlaurie@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="320892" owner_email="bfreed@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/vboot_reference" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/vboot_reference" ref="refs/changes/92/320892/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ice66a9ade7d717f87d00161545658522a09531a3" commit="ccec58abb0609634a42cfde3d93505cc97bf3c2b" commit_message="Add an Atmel specific FW updater script  This CL extracts Atmel touch FW updates from the monolithic updater script.  Atmel's update is slightly more complex than other vendors for a couple of reasons:  1. Their FW version numbers are 3-parts X.Y.Z  2. Their updater functionality in the driver accepts a FW name This new script is heavily based on the original, but has been modified for readability and can be clearer because it doesn't handle any other devices but Atmels.  BUG=chromium:525136 TEST=manually tested on Atmel touchpads and screens, upgrading, downgrading, and staying the same.  It all worked.  Since the monolithic script is unchanged, Atmel devices should be the only ones effected.  Change-Id: Ice66a9ade7d717f87d00161545658522a09531a3 Signed-off-by: Charlie Mooney &lt;charliemooney@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/315146 Reviewed-by: Andrew de los Reyes &lt;adlr@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="315146" owner_email="charliemooney@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/platform/touch_updater" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/touch_updater" ref="refs/changes/46/315146/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I86e9f325329b7ad1a4c7c5971b7851e9024e7750" commit="e0afb9c407ee4be072b34458c59a21f62daa8f54" commit_message="util: presubmit_check.sh: Fix check for ec3po.  The presubmit check would nag at the user to run the EC-3PO unit tests, even if they hadn't modified any EC-3PO files.  This was not my intention.  This commit fixes the presubmit check to only check for unit test success if a EC-3PO file is modified.  BUG=chromium:575032 BRANCH=None TEST=Remove util/ec3po/.tests-passed; Modify a non-ec3po file, commit, and try to upload.  Verify that no nag message is presented. TEST=Remove util/ec3po/.tests-passed; Modify a ec3po file, commit, and try to upload.  Verify that a nag message to run unit tests is presented.  Change-Id: I86e9f325329b7ad1a4c7c5971b7851e9024e7750 Signed-off-by: Aseda Aboagye &lt;aaboagye@google.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/320831 Commit-Ready: Aseda Aboagye &lt;aaboagye@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Aseda Aboagye &lt;aaboagye@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Shawn N &lt;shawnn@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="320831" owner_email="aaboagye@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/31/320831/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-2015.07" change_id="I15195b748213553907ff22dbc74651d70f3c7bb6" commit="3a18b6755a10ab600de6070863434174481c4ba7" commit_message="Lars: Set Correct RCOMP Target for LARs EVT boards  Below are correct RCOMP Target Values  Samsung K4E6E304EB part = {100, 40, 40, 21, 40}  Rest all DIMM should have RCOMP as {100, 40, 40, 23, 40}  LARs EVT has new DIMM added, earlier RCOMP settings was not correct for newly added DIMM cars, causing reboot issue. With this patch all DIMM gets its required value programmed.  BRANCH=None BUG=None TEST=Built for Lars EVT SKU1/2/3 and verified Boot to OS. No Reboot after this change.  Change-Id: I15195b748213553907ff22dbc74651d70f3c7bb6 Signed-off-by: Subrata Banik &lt;subrata.banik@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/320527 Reviewed-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="320527" owner_email="subrata.banik@intel.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" ref="refs/changes/27/320527/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I7dadba4d3edcffe435b2326d608549f3cf342d5d" commit="928ea8e74c127d752a08eded5650f913719764ea" commit_message="FAFT: Enabling FW repair for DUTs in faft-test-tot pool  Currently FW repair only enabled for faft-test.  Enabling for faft-test-tot pool as well as we are starting to have DUTs running there as well.  BUG=chromium:575235 BRANCH=None TEST=This will be tested in nightly testing.  Change-Id: I7dadba4d3edcffe435b2326d608549f3cf342d5d Signed-off-by: Shelley Chen &lt;shchen@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/320891 Reviewed-by: Wai-Hong Tam &lt;waihong@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="320891" owner_email="shchen@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/91/320891/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><lkgm version="7806.0.0-rc3"/></manifest>